  "process_success": true,
  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll first read the project instructions and the OpenSocrates controller, then collect the frozen source files and build a reproducible analysis that feeds the report, deck, workbook, and metrics JSON.",
    "The OpenSocrates controller selected a provenance-aware option comparison for the funding decision. I’m treating the stated €450k capex and seven-FTE limits as hard constraints; the source room’s scenario policy will establish how to compare feasible options and expose the assumptions that could change the choice.",
    "I’ve reconciled the source extracts: 1,328 raw order rows reduce to 1,297 order IDs after exact-duplicate and revision handling; 1,254 eligible 2025 shipments are valued. Returns are revision-selected and joined only to eligible original order IDs. The first scenario pass favors Czechia + Spain on base annual contribution; I’m now checking its stress downside and strongest alternatives before fixing the recommendation.",
    "The scenario comparison is now explicit: Czechia + Spain leads on the client’s base case (€198.1k annual incremental contribution; €225k capex; five FTE; 1.14-year simple payback) and remains positive in the defined joint stress (€32.2k). Netherlands + Spain is the risk-sensitive alternative: €31.2k less in the base case, but €107.6k in stress and a stronger minimum across scenarios. I’m documenting that choice and the flip condition in the artifacts.",
    "The report and deck now render as seven landscape pages/slides each. I checked the layout images and corrected the implementation page so both the 90-day gates and KPI table fit without clipping. Next I’m reconciling the saved workbook/PDF outputs against the JSON and raw archive hashes, then I’ll leave a short rebuild guide with the files.",
    "One decision point deserves a separate check: the base leader changes if the board sets a stress-case floor. I’m quantifying that flip condition against the feasible alternatives and preserving the assumption behind it in the recommendation data.",
    "The report and deck are rendered and visually checked. I’m finishing the reproducibility notes and running the final cross-check against the saved evidence, workbook, PDFs, and metrics JSON.",
    "All 16,602 independent checks pass, including source hashes, per-order conversions and rounding, monthly-to-annual reconciliation, scenario formulas, workbook checks, and the rendered PDFs. I’m doing a final inventory now so the handoff points directly to the complete deliverables and records the tooling limitation accurately.",
    "## Deliverables\n\n- [Executive report PDF](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/executive_report.pdf>) and [board presentation PDF](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/board_presentation.pdf>); editable HTML print masters and rendered previews are also included.\n- [Analytical workbook](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_analysis.xlsx>) and [metrics JSON](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/metrics.json>).\n- [Source register](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/source_register.csv>), [collected source-room files](<<CELL>/workspace/evidence/source_room/index.html>), and [rebuild and verification instructions](<<CELL>/workspace/analysis/README.md>).\n\nThe recommendation is to stage Czechia and Spain within **€225,000 capex and 5 FTE**, opening Spain first and making the Czechia tranche conditional on the implementation gates. Their estimated annual incremental contribution is **€64.6k low, €198.1k base, €331.6k high, and €32.2k under the defined stress**. These are scenario calculations from synthetic client records and assumptions, not proven hub effects.\n\nThe independent verifier passed **16,602 checks** across source hashes, accounting, FX, scenario arithmetic, workbook reconciliations, PDFs, and previews. PDF pages and slides were visually inspected. The workbook was structurally checked, but an Excel or LibreOffice rendering check was unavailable. The report and README document the synthetic inputs, source vintage, assumptions, and other material limitations.\n\nOpenSocrates grounding: trade-off-analysis@3, sensitivity-analysis@3"
  ],
  "final": "## Deliverables\n\n- [Executive report PDF](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/executive_report.pdf>) and [board presentation PDF](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/board_presentation.pdf>); editable HTML print masters and rendered previews are also included.\n- [Analytical workbook](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_analysis.xlsx>) and [metrics JSON](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/metrics.json>).\n- [Source register](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/source_register.csv>), [collected source-room files](<<CELL>/workspace/evidence/source_room/index.html>), and [rebuild and verification instructions](<<CELL>/workspace/analysis/README.md>).\n\nThe recommendation is to stage Czechia and Spain within **€225,000 capex and 5 FTE**, opening Spain first and making the Czechia tranche conditional on the implementation gates. Their estimated annual incremental contribution is **€64.6k low, €198.1k base, €331.6k high, and €32.2k under the defined stress**. These are scenario calculations from synthetic client records and assumptions, not proven hub effects.\n\nThe independent verifier passed **16,602 checks** across source hashes, accounting, FX, scenario arithmetic, workbook reconciliations, PDFs, and previews. PDF pages and slides were visually inspected. The workbook was structurally checked, but an Excel or LibreOffice rendering check was unavailable. The report and README document the synthetic inputs, source vintage, assumptions, and other material limitations.\n\nOpenSocrates grounding: trade-off-analysis@3, sensitivity-analysis@3",
